WEBVTT

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:10.620
Well, the question we had to ask ourselves from the very beginning was could a group

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:13.740
of skateboarders pull off opening their own park?

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:19.170
Was it possible for us to organize this, build this, manage it, actually make it happen?

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:07.670
Growing up in Hawaii, we were forced into skateboarding in drainage ditches, schools,

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:09.670
pools, shopping centers.

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:13.670
There was never really anywhere legal for us to skate, so we just went anywhere we could go.

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:18.580
Yeah, it's like, in what key, you can't go skateboarding.

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:22.580
I mean, all these ditches, like pipeline bowls, they demolished.

00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:25.480
Wallows is messed up.

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:30.000
A lot of the older spots are non-skateable now, or they're all messed up.

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:35.380
up so I think it's time for Hawaii to build new skate spots and maybe parks is the way

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:37.400
to go this time around.

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:41.410
The city did make an attempt to accommodate the needs of the skateboarders.

00:01:41.410 --> 00:01:47.130
In 1988 Mayor Fosse planned to build 12 skate parks across Oahu, four were built, two are

00:01:47.130 --> 00:01:48.090
already gone.

00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:54.250
But we also have two concrete skate parks and one in Ewa Beach area and the other one

00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:57.840
in Waianae area which were built in the late 80s.

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:00.000
The problem with Ewa and Waianae was that it was two

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:06.000
convenient for us. We lived in Hawaii Kai, and most of the skateboarders lived in Honolulu.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:09.720
We probably went out there four or five times a year.

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:17.760
The skate parks around here, before this park opened, were not on the, really, they weren't

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:27.190
on the good side of things, you know? They just sucked, basically. They were built for

00:02:27.190 --> 00:02:29.280
skateboarders by friends.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:37.160
park and recreation type officials which had no clue what the sport was about and we needed

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:41.790
a park built by skateboarders for skateboarders.

00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:48.370
I think it was in 1996 I was attending a meeting in Kailua and at the meeting was a skate park

00:02:48.370 --> 00:02:52.990
designer named Ken Warmout from the mainland and he designed Derby skate park, Santa Rosa,

00:02:52.990 --> 00:03:00.000
Palo Alto and a few other skate parks up there and what he had to say was really interesting about how

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:04.860
they build skate parks up there and etc but to me the most interesting thing at

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:08.670
that meeting was the fact that they announced that there was a place of

00:03:08.670 --> 00:03:13.080
property called kapohu that might be available for kids to put their

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:17.420
skateboard ramps on the weekends and skate and when I heard about that I saw

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:21.360
that as an opportunity for some of the older skateboarders in the community to

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:25.880
make a real skate park something that that we wanted something that we knew

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:30.000
the kids would skate a new skate park will be opened under the freeway at high

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:35.240
Harding in Cappahula, and as Terry Hunter reports, it took two years to make this park

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:36.240
a reality.

00:03:36.240 --> 00:04:00.000
Once I knew the land was available, and once I knew the city was willing

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:04.740
cooperate I knew that it was up to us to make this happen it was up to us to get

00:04:04.740 --> 00:04:10.850
organized and it meant going to meetings talking with city members talking to

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:15.680
council members talking to all kinds of people and I knew that if we were just a

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:19.040
bunch of skaters strolling in there saying yeah we want a skate park we want

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:22.590
this this and this that they wouldn't listen to us so the only way for them to

00:04:22.590 --> 00:04:27.320
take us seriously was for us to get organized and that's what we did we

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:30.000
established the Hawaii Skate Park Association

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:35.760
And it was this organization that became the speaking voice for the skateboarders in Hawaii.

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:38.780
In order to acquire the land at Kapahula, we needed two things.

00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:43.180
The first thing was a federal nonprofit status, and the second thing was insurance.

00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:47.800
And we, as the Hawaii Skate Park Association, needed to work in conjunction with a larger

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:49.880
organization in order to accomplish that.

00:04:49.880 --> 00:04:58.880
We were first approached by Mr. Kevin Buckley, who is the president of the Hawaii Skate Park

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:00.000
Association.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:09.940
provided us with a business proposal on their plan to establish a skate park and they needed

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:15.180
some collaborative efforts on the community side to get this thing started.

00:05:15.180 --> 00:05:23.130
Basically, the YMC is here to provide for the needs of the people in our community and

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:28.080
the skate park fit in because, as you know, we're in the Waikiki area where skateboarders

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:30.000
and inline skaters.

00:05:30.090 --> 00:05:36.140
have been banned from actually riding in the area, and so this was a great opportunity

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:40.110
for the YMCA to get involved in providing for the need of those people.

00:05:40.110 --> 00:05:47.160
They had a very clear plan, very clear objectives, and basically what they needed from the YMCA

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:49.960
was its programming strengths.

00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:54.400
Now that the YMCA was involved, there was only two small things we needed to do to get

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:55.900
the park open.

00:05:55.900 --> 00:06:00.000
The first thing we needed to do was get approvals from the federal government

00:06:00.120 --> 00:06:02.890
from the city and from the state government.

00:06:02.890 --> 00:06:06.630
The second small thing we needed to do was needed to get the funds.

00:06:06.630 --> 00:06:10.150
In order to get the approvals from the city, state and federal governments, we needed to

00:06:10.150 --> 00:06:14.130
meet with these officials and show them how we're going to operate the skate park.

00:06:14.130 --> 00:06:20.730
Once we met them, they started actually making it look concrete and they then became the

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:24.950
voice that went to the community and started convincing them because they were the skaters.

00:06:24.950 --> 00:06:30.000
They're the ones that everybody was complaining about in their communities and then these

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:32.440
that young men showed up at these community meetings

00:06:32.440 --> 00:06:34.750
and said, this is what we want to do,

00:06:34.750 --> 00:06:37.870
and here's how we're gonna stop some of the bad behavior

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:40.890
that you, the community, is complaining about.

00:06:40.890 --> 00:06:43.590
This is what this park is gonna do for your community.

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:45.930
They were able to do the convincing.

00:06:45.930 --> 00:06:48.040
- Now that all the paperwork was intact,

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:52.370
all we needed to do was get the funds, build the ramps,

00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:54.740
and set an opening date.

00:06:54.740 --> 00:06:56.440
There were a lot of things that we could have done

00:06:56.440 --> 00:06:58.110
that I knew would have taken anywhere

00:06:58.110 --> 00:07:00.000
from six months to an extra year,

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:04.800
before we could open and at that point the YMCA said you know what Kevin we

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:11.560
need to open this park let's get it open send us a wood list and let's set an

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:16.620
opening date and let's do it and that's exactly what we did well there's been

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:21.070
parks opening up in Hawaii over the past like 10 15 years but it's nothing

00:07:21.070 --> 00:07:25.250
really that I really wanted to ride or anything that I really like so I decided

00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:30.000
if I could make a difference and help out building obstacles that could help

00:07:30.700 --> 00:07:35.120
I guess the skaters progress in Hawaii, then I would take that chance and the opportunity

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:38.050
and just help out and do it.

00:07:38.050 --> 00:07:43.140
For months I've been telling my friends and the skateboarders in Hawaii that we're going

00:07:43.140 --> 00:07:46.800
to have this park, we're going to open this park, we're going to build this park.

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:53.110
And then one day I invited 15 of them down to the skate park and I showed them two humongous

00:07:53.110 --> 00:07:59.270
stacks of wood, plywood, 2x4s, 2x6s, nails, everything, we had tools.

00:08:00.280 --> 00:08:05.700
I said we're opening up in two weekends, let's start building.

00:08:05.700 --> 00:08:10.880
The freeway overhead will keep skaters relatively dry on a rainy day, the city laid fresh pavement

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:16.360
for the 20,000 square foot course that includes wooden obstacles, ramps, boxes, quarter pipes

00:08:16.360 --> 00:08:17.960
for stunts and maneuvering.

00:08:17.960 --> 00:08:20.380
The YMCA will manage the park for the city.

00:08:20.380 --> 00:08:24.340
We're trying to provide positive things for the kids to do so they don't get involved

00:08:24.340 --> 00:08:25.340
in drugs and gangs.

00:08:25.340 --> 00:08:30.000
And one of the things that they love is skating, so this is our first skateboard facility.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:32.960
and it's a tribute to people working together.

00:08:32.960 --> 00:08:34.620
We got the land from the federal government,

00:08:34.620 --> 00:08:36.320
we have the YMCA participating,

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:38.140
the neighborhood board, and the kids.

00:08:38.140 --> 00:08:40.500
The kids actually did most of the construction.

00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:42.520
- The city plans other similar facilities

00:08:42.520 --> 00:08:45.020
around the island in Pearl City and on the North Shore,

00:08:45.020 --> 00:08:47.880
and it plans to turn a park and ride facility

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:51.110
in Hawaii Kai into an inline hockey facility.

00:08:51.110 --> 00:08:53.910
- See, the Kapu Hulu Skate Park is portable,

00:08:53.910 --> 00:08:57.100
so the advantages are you can set it up differently

00:08:57.100 --> 00:09:00.000
every weekend and have change and different things to skate

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:05.080
different ways to skate it, but the disadvantages of it is it's got to be small and mobile.

00:09:05.080 --> 00:09:09.240
One of the problems with the Kapahulu Skate Park is that we have to set it up and break

00:09:09.240 --> 00:09:10.240
it down every weekend.

00:09:10.240 --> 00:09:15.340
What this means is that our volunteers have to come in there Friday night and set the

00:09:15.340 --> 00:09:19.700
park up in a particular way and on Sunday after the park closes we have to flip all

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:22.150
the ramps up and bring them back.

00:09:39.080 --> 00:09:44.070
In the first 18 months of the opening of the Kapaluhu Skate Park, we have over 600 members.

00:09:44.070 --> 00:09:49.150
We're working on programs right now to train the little kids just on etiquette and the

00:09:49.150 --> 00:09:50.910
basics of skateboarding.

00:09:50.910 --> 00:09:58.410
We've had skateboard contests from just about every skateboard business on the island.

00:09:58.410 --> 00:10:00.000
We had demonstrations.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:05.180
Several companies from the mainland, professionals coming down, skating at our park.

00:10:05.730 --> 00:10:10.090
Well, the scene in Hawaii is definitely growing just because there's people from out of town coming in.

00:10:10.570 --> 00:10:14.300
And we have a place to meet now and skateboard together.

00:10:15.160 --> 00:10:18.960
Before, there wasn't really a designated area to go skateboarding.

00:10:19.360 --> 00:10:26.710
Now we're skating frequently with a lot of people who we just used to see and not even know their names.

00:10:26.710 --> 00:10:29.250
You know, we would skate at the same spot with them.

00:10:30.090 --> 00:10:34.530
but we wouldn't really talk to them and stuff and now it just brings everybody together.

00:10:34.530 --> 00:11:00.000
Since the opening of the Kapahulu Skate Park we've seen a lot of things happen as far as

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:05.710
is concerned in Hawaii. One, there was a new cement park built in Kaneohe. There's a new

00:11:05.710 --> 00:11:11.910
cement park built in Maui. Hikam Air Force Base has redesigned their entire park to meet

00:11:11.910 --> 00:11:18.660
today's standards of skateboarding. And what I would like to see in the future is Kapuhulu

00:11:18.660 --> 00:11:26.060
expanding. Hopefully we'll get our vert ramp soon and lights for night skating and maybe

00:11:26.060 --> 00:11:30.000
a bigger street course. We've seen a huge growth in skateboarders

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:31.300
and inline skaters in Hawaii

00:11:31.300 --> 00:11:34.300
and I don't think this is due to

00:11:34.300 --> 00:11:35.820
the fact that Kapohulu opened

00:11:35.820 --> 00:11:37.480
I think it was due to the fact that

00:11:37.480 --> 00:11:39.660
there was just more facilities for them to use

00:11:39.660 --> 00:11:41.380
It's been very

00:11:41.380 --> 00:11:43.080
eye-opening

00:11:43.080 --> 00:11:45.670
on how to get through the system

00:11:45.670 --> 00:11:47.090
and get these kind of things done

00:11:47.090 --> 00:11:48.730
I would like to see

00:11:48.730 --> 00:11:51.350
more of the concrete

00:11:51.350 --> 00:11:53.810
street type

00:11:53.810 --> 00:11:55.270
linear type courses

00:11:55.270 --> 00:11:58.200
It's all about having something that we want to ride

00:11:58.200 --> 00:11:59.540
being able to

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:02.180
and do something that we want to do.

00:12:02.180 --> 00:12:04.650
And it's like, at least we can honestly say

00:12:04.650 --> 00:12:07.350
we're making a difference instead of doing nothing about it.

00:12:07.350 --> 00:12:12.300
- 'Cause I think that's what sold this to the community,

00:12:12.300 --> 00:12:17.540
was some very young 18, 19, 20, 24 year olds.

00:12:17.540 --> 00:12:20.280
That's the group that really sold this project.

00:12:20.280 --> 00:12:22.310
And so it can be done.

00:12:22.310 --> 00:12:24.890
- I would like to see them be able to get the entire lot,

00:12:24.890 --> 00:12:27.240
not have to set up and break down every weekend.

00:12:27.240 --> 00:12:30.000
I would like to see it maybe even relocate to a warehouse

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:34.380
facility where we don't have to worry about weather and opening up only on

00:12:34.380 --> 00:12:39.450
weekends and setting up and breaking down. And what it boils down to is this. The

00:12:39.450 --> 00:12:43.880
park is for us, the skateboarders of Hawaii. It's a place for us to skate

00:12:43.880 --> 00:12:48.940
legally. Skatepark was like an experiment to test average skateboarders to see if

00:12:48.940 --> 00:12:53.260
they could actually organize such a project, build the facility and manage it.

00:12:53.260 --> 00:12:59.350
We've done that and from our experiences we believe that it can be done anywhere.

00:13:05.530 --> 00:13:05.970
Thank you.

00:14:30.120 --> 00:14:31.090
Bye.
